WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.950
A small spring launcher.

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.390
Push the spring in,
load a ball, and let go.

3
00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.720
The spring hands the ball its
stored energy: 0.25 joules.

4
00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:14.080
Stretching or squashing
a spring takes work.

5
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.360
In the elastic region,
you get that work back.

6
00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:19.290
So here is the puzzle.

7
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.740
Stretch a spring twice as far.

8
00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:24.080
Does it store twice the energy?

9
00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:28.300
In this mission, you'll link the energy
stored in a spring to its force against

10
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.910
extension graph.

11
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.600
Then you'll push a wire beyond
its limit of proportionality,

12
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:35.680
where the graph starts to curve.

13
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:40.390
Your mission: predict how much energy the
spring stores when you stretch it twice

14
00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.170
as far.
